The remaining slack is in stage 3. I move the `c1` constant out of `q`. The term `xt*c1` is now a plaintext multiply on the shallow `x*t`, so it is cheap and sits at a low level. The plaintext add on the `a` branch goes away. The `c5` plaintext add stays in `b`, which is the deepest branch.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext t = x;
  for (int stage = 1; stage <= 2; ++stage)
  {
    string p = "s" + to_string(stage) + "c";
    Plaintext c1(p + "1"), c3(p + "3"), c5(p + "5"), c7(p + "7");
    Ciphertext u = square(t);
    Ciphertext u2 = square(u);
    Ciphertext low = t * c1 + (t * c3) * u;
    Ciphertext high = t * c5 + (t * c7) * u;
    t = low + high * u2;
  }
  Plaintext c1("s3c1"), c3("s3c3"), c5("s3c5"), c7("s3c7"), half("half");
  Ciphertext u = square(t);
  Ciphertext u2 = square(u);
  Ciphertext xt = x * t;
  Ciphertext b = u * c7 + c5;
  Ciphertext q = u * c3 + b * u2;
  Ciphertext y = xt * q + (xt * c1 + x * half);
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

This attempt changes only the order of additions in stages 1 and 2. I add the deepest term first, and the shallow terms `(t*c3)*u` and `t*c1` are merged afterward at lower levels. The aim is to cut the level and scale alignments CHEHAB inserts. Stage 3 stays as in attempt 3.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext t = x;
  for (int stage = 1; stage <= 2; ++stage)
  {
    string p = "s" + to_string(stage) + "c";
    Plaintext c1(p + "1"), c3(p + "3"), c5(p + "5"), c7(p + "7");
    Ciphertext u = square(t);
    Ciphertext u2 = square(u);
    Ciphertext high = (t * c7) * u + t * c5;
    Ciphertext r = high * u2;
    Ciphertext m = (t * c3) * u;
    Ciphertext s = r + m;
    t = s + t * c1;
  }
  Plaintext c1("s3c1"), c3("s3c3"), c5("s3c5"), c7("s3c7"), half("half");
  Ciphertext u = square(t);
  Ciphertext u2 = square(u);
  Ciphertext xt = x * t;
  Ciphertext a = u * c3 + c1;
  Ciphertext b = u * c7 + c5;
  Ciphertext q = a + b * u2;
  Ciphertext y = xt * q + x * half;
  y.set_output("y");
}
```

With one attempt left, I'm trying a mixed form. Stage 1 uses the reordered additions from attempt 7. Stage 2 keeps the baseline grouping, and stage 3 keeps the regrouped `(x*t)*q` form. I don't expect a large change.

```cpp
void fhe()
{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Ciphertext t = x;
  for (int stage = 1; stage <= 2; ++stage)
  {
    string p = "s" + to_string(stage) + "c";
    Plaintext c1(p + "1"), c3(p + "3"), c5(p + "5"), c7(p + "7");
    Ciphertext u = square(t);
    Ciphertext u2 = square(u);
    if (stage == 1)
    {
      Ciphertext high = (t * c7) * u + t * c5;
      Ciphertext s = high * u2 + (t * c3) * u;
      t = s + t * c1;
    }
    else
    {
      Ciphertext low = t * c1 + (t * c3) * u;
      Ciphertext high = t * c5 + (t * c7) * u;
      t = low + high * u2;
    }
  }
  Plaintext c1("s3c1"), c3("s3c3"), c5("s3c5"), c7("s3c7"), half("half");
  Ciphertext u = square(t);
  Ciphertext u2 = square(u);
  Ciphertext xt = x * t;
  Ciphertext a = u * c3 + c1;
  Ciphertext b = u * c7 + c5;
  Ciphertext q = a + b * u2;
  Ciphertext y = xt * q + x * half;
  y.set_output("y");
}
